From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Mower <mdmower@cmphys.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:50:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [bugs #3727] Propagate kills through non-dominating
 predecessors in the data flow

The incoming expressions of each block are those of its dominating
predecessor minus what its other predecessors kill. That test only
looked at what each such predecessor kills itself. For

    n1 = 0;
    if (bad)
      for (j = 0; j < 1; j++)
        fake ();          /* sets n1 */
    use (2 * n1);

the call removes 'n1 = 0' from the loop header's incoming expressions,
but the block after the loop is reached from the header, which contains
no call, so 'n1 = 0' remained there and n1 was replaced by 0.

Record what is deleted during the merge in the block's killed
expressions, which are already propagated to successors and consulted by
the test.

Enables the assertion in tests/bug-3727.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/SDCCdflow.c                     | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 support/regression/tests/bug-3727.c |  6 +-----
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/SDCCdflow.c b/src/SDCCdflow.c
index e8707626a..2f382fb33 100644
--- a/src/SDCCdflow.c
+++ b/src/SDCCdflow.c
@@ -27,12 +27,11 @@
 #include "common.h"
 
 /*-----------------------------------------------------------------*/
-/* ifKilledInBlock - will return 1 if the symbol is redefined in B */
+/* killedInBlock - will return 1 if the symbol is redefined in B   */
 /*-----------------------------------------------------------------*/
-DEFSETFUNC (ifKilledInBlock)
+static int
+killedInBlock (cseDef *cdp, eBBlock *src)
 {
-  cseDef *cdp = item;
-  V_ARG (eBBlock *, src);
   bitVect *outs;
 
   /* if this is a global variable and this block
@@ -90,6 +89,17 @@ DEFSETFUNC (ifKilledInBlock)
   return 0;
 }
 
+/*-----------------------------------------------------------------*/
+/* ifKilledInBlock - set function form of killedInBlock            */
+/*-----------------------------------------------------------------*/
+DEFSETFUNC (ifKilledInBlock)
+{
+  cseDef *cdp = item;
+  V_ARG (eBBlock *, src);
+
+  return killedInBlock (cdp, src);
+}
+
 /*-----------------------------------------------------------------*/
 /* mergeInExprs - copy the in expression if it dominates           */
 /*-----------------------------------------------------------------*/
@@ -126,6 +136,16 @@ DEFSETFUNC (mergeInExprs)
       //if (dest != ebp)
       //  dest->inExprs = intersectSets (dest->inExprs, ebp->outExprs, THROW_DEST);
 
+      cseDef *cdp;
+
+      /* What this predecessor kills is killed for the blocks after dest as well, when they are
+         reached from dest without passing through their own dominator again: remember it.
+         Otherwise a call in a loop body removes a global from the loop header's incoming
+         expressions, but not from those of the block the loop exits to (bug #3727). */
+      for (cdp = setFirstItem (dest->inExprs); cdp; cdp = setNextItem (dest->inExprs))
+        if (killedInBlock (cdp, ebp) && !isinSetWith (dest->killedExprs, cdp, isCseDefEqual))
+          addSetHead (&dest->killedExprs, cdp);
+
       /* delete only if killed in this block*/
       deleteItemIf (&dest->inExprs, ifKilledInBlock, ebp);
       /* union the ndompset with pointers set in this block */
diff --git a/support/regression/tests/bug-3727.c b/support/regression/tests/bug-3727.c
index d72118f74..ba027b88b 100644
--- a/support/regression/tests/bug-3727.c
+++ b/support/regression/tests/bug-3727.c
@@ -39,10 +39,6 @@ void testBug(void)
 
 void VDP_Poke_16K( u8 dest )
 {
-#if 0 // Bug not yet fixed
-    ASSERT(dest);
-#else
-    (void)dest;
-#endif
+    ASSERT(dest == 64);
 }
 
